/target
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Built packages: the plain bundle, the signed copy the sandbox is measured
# against, the universal one, the Store package, and the Developer ID build the
# arm64 walkthrough carries — a Store build cannot be launched off the Store, so
# the walkthrough needs a different certificate. Every one of them is assembled
# by `packaging/macos/build-app.sh` from what is committed. Deliberately not
# counted here: this comment said "All three" while listing four.
dist/
dist-sandboxed/
dist-universal/
dist-store/
dist-devid/

# `make-ico` is its own package, so its build directory is its own too and the
# root-anchored rule above does not reach it.
/packaging/windows/make-ico/target/

# The Mac App Store submission walkthrough, which names the account, the team,
# and the certificates. `packaging/macos/README.md` carries everything about the
# bundle that belongs on a public record; this one is deliberately local, and
# `git log` shows what taking an account identifier back out of a public
# repository costs.
/packaging/macos/SUBMITTING.local.md

# The Windows package identity Partner Center assigned. Not a credential —
# `Publisher` is in the manifest of every package the Store distributes and the
# store id is in the public listing URL — but it is an account's identifiers on
# a public record, which is the same judgement the macOS file above got.
# `identity.psd1.example` beside it is committed and says what goes in.
/packaging/windows/identity.psd1

# The Microsoft Store submission walkthrough, which names the store id and the
# Azure AD application the submission API will use. Same judgement as the macOS
# file above: `packaging/windows/README.md` carries everything about the package
# that belongs on a public record, and this one is deliberately local.
/packaging/windows/SUBMITTING.local.md
